            H3("The performance measurement baseline"),
            "The PMI Lexicon defines the **performance measurement baseline (PMB)** as the \"integrated scope, schedule, and cost baselines used for comparison to manage, measure, and control project execution\". Integration is the point: every work package has an agreed scope, a planned time window and a budget, so earned value can compare the value of work done (EV) with the value of work planned (PV) and the cost incurred (AC). The [earned value management](/project-management/earned-value-management/) guide covers those formulas in full.",
            "Formal earned value management systems used on US government contracts define the PMB slightly differently. The US Department of Defense EVM glossary describes it as a time-phased, resourced plan made up of all distributed budget plus undistributed budget, with management reserve held outside it. The idea is the same; the vocabulary is more detailed because contracts need it.",
